        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مر (murr) is built on the native Arabic root m-r-r, \"to be bitter\" (Lane). English myrrh, the bitter resin, came through Greek from a Semitic word of this kind; Hebrew mar, \"bitter\", is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
